  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If you have Audio Listener setup with a Reverb/Echo filter inside a world, normally you'd be able to make audio source components not be affected by enabling \"Bypass Listener Effects\". While it works perfectly fine in-editor with the Client Simulator, it completely ignores the bypass in-game.\n\nI'm mainly trying to make a \"Music\" audio source not be affected by reverb/echo while allowing other sources (including player voices) to be affected.",
